			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_583935635494115575">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475596239', '807973945275927412', '583935635494110426', '39889344', '583935635494115575' );" data-tooltip-text="Denunciar este mensaje por contenido inapropiado. Los mensajes denunciados son marcados para que sean revisados por los moderadores.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Denunciar este mensaje</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_583935635494115575">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Publicado originalmente por <b><a href="#c583935635494111793">CyberDown</a></b>:</div>Meanwhile real humans unable to recreate the magic in mmorpgs that happened 20-25 years ago.  But its popular to hate AI so people do.  Only chance we have getting a good mmorpg will be due to AI and lack of investors. </blockquote><br>The reason they'll never be able to do that is because you're not 14 anymore, no MMO is ever going to recreate it.<br>You can't recreate your first time.<br><br> There's good reasons to hate generative ai... It's built on theft and parasites off of artists the same people who make these games...<br>It's just bizarre to defend it, because you're not defending creatives you're defending corporate who want to replace people to save a buck.<br>The people who actually make the games pretty much universally don't want to use this ♥♥♥♥ and are forced to.<br><br> It's strange how some people defend gen ai being used so hard when all that is happening is you're being given a lower quality product so a CEO can buy another yacht.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
