			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_583936001036119927">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Publicado originalmente por <b><a href="#c583935635494111793">CyberDown</a></b>:</div>Meanwhile real humans unable to recreate the magic in mmorpgs that happened 20-25 years ago.  But its popular to hate AI so people do.  Only chance we have getting a good mmorpg will be due to AI and lack of investors. </blockquote><br>That's because the only ones motivated by that are frauds who just want to put out a playable version and then sell it as early access and run off with all the money. It happens all the time and triple A studios don't care about that, it's infinitely more profitable to release some mobile game with whales. <br><br>Those games earns billions per year just from microtransactions alone, FF14 really is the only one left that's a proper MMO and not ruined by all this.<br><br>I have plans and I know there's a vet dev team out there working on something too but it's all too early to even mention anything.			</div>
