				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Denunciar este mensaje</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_583936001036122528">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Publicado originalmente por <b><a href="#c583935635494114463">NC CM Sakaar</a></b>:</div>We answered this recently in this thread:<br><a class="bb_link" href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/3393110/discussions/1/583935003344372119/" target="_blank" rel="" >https://steamcommunity.com/app/3393110/discussions/1/583935003344372119/</a></blockquote><br>Some people are deaf and blind.<br>They think they are intelligent, and for some reason, are trying to compete with Ai...<br><br>But thank you for clearing that up for everyone that can understand basic English.<br><br>Ai is the devil to so many people - not because they care about humanity, creativity, or even Armageddon...<br><br>But because it shows them up.  <br>From chat bots, to music, to art, to video gen...  Ai is a tool.  <br>And used responsibly, is an asset.<br><br>But people are too often the problem.  And technology always gets scape-goated.<br><br>Turning the world into a bunch of angry Villagers, trying to burn Frankenstein's monster - again...<br>Utterly blind to the fact ethics and integrity are human concepts.<br><br>Some of us appreciate the work that was put in, regardless.  <br>Thanks again.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
